From: awto-tl-st1008f
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: aquantia: clamp hwmon limits instead of -ERANGE (#124)

The thermal core programs set_trips(-INT_MAX, ...) when no trip lies below the current
temperature; aqr_hwmon_set() rejected it with -ERANGE ("Failed to set trips: -34") before
temp_max was written. Clamp to the register's s16 range, as hwmon expects of limit writes.
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_hwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_hwmon.c
@@ -56,8 +56,8 @@
 {
 	int temp;
 
-	if (value >= 128000 || value < -128000)
-		return -ERANGE;
+	/* s16, LSB = 1/256 degC: clamp like other hwmon limit writes (thermal core passes -INT_MAX) */
+	value = clamp_val(value, -128000, 127996);
 
 	temp = value * 256 / 1000;
 
